  "maxVersionNote": "1.0.19 13/10/2026: the dark half of every light-dark() whose light half reads the slot reads it too (darkArms, feat/ds-every-template-3), so a dark system no longer shows the template's own dark colours; unworn, both halves compute what they did. 1.0.12 to 1.0.16 checked 11/10/2026 (ds-minversion-audit): the same 6 var(--ds-c- reads and tracy_apply_inspiration as 1.0.11; their css changes are words (CSS content) and fonts, no colour; 1.0.17 checked 12/10/2026 (published-templates-green): the same var(--ds-*) reads as 1.0.16 and tracy_apply_inspiration kept; every role class is still drawn by the theme or the demo; the theme change is words, dates, fonts and links, no colour 13/10/2026: 1.0.18 = 1.0.17 with the theme's other stylesheets tokenized (TDSR CSS-2, fix/tdsr-css2); measured with flow.mjs before release. 1.0.20 16/10/2026 (#1375): a status colour set as text (the shared sections' plan ticks and form notes, the theme's own .text-danger, .text-success and required marks) reads the readable shade the slot makes for the worn page (--ds-c-<status>-text); unworn, every value is the theme's own. 1.0.21 19/10/2026 (dot 3, feat/ds-dot3-a2): the theme reads every standard role variable itself (var(--ds-*, <its own value>), role scan 0 unresolved, design-system-roles.json on quickstart 1.0.19), unworn the same computed styles as 1.0.20 on 40 pages; shipped in quickstart/ja-essence/wp7 1.0.19. 1.0.22 21/10/2026 (TEXT-1): five outline-button text colours on the typography page (assets/css/je-detail.css) read --ds-c-on-ink instead of a ground role; unworn, the same computed styles on every page that carries them; shipped in quickstart/ja-essence/wp7 1.0.20.",
