  "displayNote": "no display role: the home has no hero title, and the largest heading near the top is a post card's title (32px, one of six). Re-measured 11/10/2026: as display, every card title took the system's display size (Moxie 55px, Toggl Track 60px) while the heading role, also a card title, wanted the heading size. The card titles are headings: they take the heading size with the section titles",
  "selectorsNote": "19/10/2026 (theme 1.0.21): the primary button role leaves the footer's dark button (.je-btn-dark, Become a subscriber) to the theme, which now paints it from the ink and raised-ground roles itself: worn as the accent it was the lightest fill of the dark page (button-dark, BTN-1). Sidebar titles (14/10/2026, look review v6): the article page's sidebar widgets (.je-side: Follow us, Trending, the newsletter) title with the same h2.je-sec__title the sections use, which the template sets at 24px there against 40px for a section; under a system they took the section heading size (up to 50px in a 300px column). The heading role stops at .je-side.",
