  "ready": true,
  "readyNote": "re-measured again 12/10/2026 with the final probe, every heading, text and block of text judged (tasks/evidence/ds-remeasure-6-2026-10-11/wordpress-ja-essence): 12/12 on every release measured, controls 0 differences, lowest text 4.70:1, 81% or more of the page follows, no text under 4.5:1 worse than the template's own, dark- and light-system screenshots read by a person. Before that: re-measured 11/10/2026 with the per-element probe on theme 1.0.11 (its minVersion) over the ja-essence/wp7 1.0.16 content (tasks/evidence/ds-remeasure-6-2026-10-11/wordpress-ja-essence): 12/12 with Moxie, MotherDuck, Toggl Track and Apple, controls 0 differences, lowest text 6.05:1, 81-95% of the page follows, screenshots read by a person. The new probe first found the pagination (#000) and the cards' Read more (#252424) black on a dark system's page (1.00-1.12:1): they take the system's text (followRules, now written by the WordPress variation too); and the heading role missed its size, because the card titles were the display role: they are headings now (displayNote). First measured 09/10/2026 (tasks/evidence/ds-slot-released-2026-10-09/templates/ja-essence-wp7)",
  "followRulesNote": "13/10/2026: the pagination and Read more were black (#000, #252424) on the template's page, its strongest ink; the worn texts follow the template's own order of strength (textOrder), where JA Essence's strongest is --fg-2, so they take fg-2 (under MotherDuck, fg read 4.01:1 on the pagination box).",
  "contractNotes1317": "13/10/2026 (#1317): the category badges, the drawer toggle, the nav labels and the media icons kept the template ink and paper; they follow. The white post titles on the cover overlays (36 left paints under Moxie) are words on photos: the template design, not a contract fix.",
